Package: rtemis.ml
Title: Performance Metrics for Classification
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-11-10
Authors@R: c(
    person(given = "E.D.", family = "Gennatas", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
           email = "gennatas@gmail.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9280-3609")),
    person(given = "Authors of the bundled Rust crates", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
           comment = "Rust crates compiled into the package; see inst/AUTHORS")
    )
Description: Computes the area under the receiver operating characteristic
    curve (AUC) and the average precision of binary classifiers, and their
    one-vs-rest values for each class of a multiclass outcome. The AUC is the
    Mann-Whitney U statistic divided by the number of positive-negative pairs
    (Hanley and McNeil (1982) <doi:10.1148/radiology.143.1.7063747>), and the
    average precision is the area under the stepwise precision-recall curve.
    The computations are implemented in the 'rtemis' 'Rust' crate, which sorts
    the scores once per problem and reads the inputs without copying them.
URL: https://www.rtemis.org, https://github.com/rtemis-org/rtemis.ml
